<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22626" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incŭbātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		incubo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a lying upon eggs</i> (in order to hatch them), <i>a brooding</i>, <i>incubation.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incubationi datur initium post novam lunam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					10, 54, 75, § 152</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">noxia ovis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 56, 77, § 156</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">derelicta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 60, 80, § 166</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>an unlawful
				possession</i>: diuturna, Cod. Th. 10. 1, 15; <i><span class="en">id.
				Just. 7, 38, 3</span></i>.</div>
